<addAttributes>
    <att name='institution'>Hakai Institute</att>
    <att name='title'>Water Property Measurements from the Bute Inlet Ocean Observing Station (BIOOS) Wirewalker, Bute Inlet, BC, Canada (Provisional)</att>
    <att name='summary'>The Bute Inlet Ocean Observing Station (BIOOS) provides high-resolution profiling in Bute Inlet, a fjord on the British Columbia coast. A C-PROOF (Canadian Pacific Robotic Ocean Observing Facility) Wirewalker, a wave-powered profiler, is moored in the central fjord, measuring conductivity, temperature, pressure, and dissolved oxygen through the water column. Two versions of the record are included: provisional data offloaded directly from the instrument, which is the more complete, and real-time data received via satellite, which is the more current.</att>
    <att name='project'>Oceanography</att>
    <att name='comment'>##Limitations:
Haven’t applied appropriate QC on the data yet.</att>
    <att name='progress'>tentative</att>
